---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Work" description="Case studies showing how I help businesses find clarity">
  <section class="hero-small">
    <h1>Work that <span class="highlight">changed things</span>.</h1>
    <p>Each project started with confusion. Each ended with clarity.</p>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <div class="work-grid">
      
      <!-- The Stack -->
      <article class="work-card">
        <div class="work-tenets">
          <span class="tenet">Clarity</span>
          <span class="tenet">AI</span>
        </div>
        <h2>The Stack</h2>
        <p class="work-subtitle">Investigative journalism reimagined for 2026</p>
        <p class="work-description">
          "Why does Times Radio lose £15M a year — and why is that genius?" 
          I took 70 pages of research from 3 AI models, found the hidden thesis, 
          and built a 3-layer story readers can skim, read, or audit.
        </p>
        <div class="work-outcome">
          <strong>Outcome:</strong> New storytelling format with depth layers, evidence chips, every claim sourced.
        </div>
        <div class="work-links">
          <a href="/case-studies/the-stack" class="case-link">Full Case Study →</a>
          <a href="/demos/the-stack/" target="_blank" class="demo-link">View Demo ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      
      <!-- Data Detectives -->
      <article class="work-card">
        <div class="work-tenets">
          <span class="tenet">Story</span>
          <span class="tenet">Clarity</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Data Detectives</h2>
        <p class="work-subtitle">A business fable on breaking silos</p>
        <p class="work-description">
          How do you teach complex organisational change in a way people actually want to read?
          I wrote a 20-chapter business fable about a team transforming data chaos into clarity.
        </p>
        <div class="work-outcome">
          <strong>Outcome:</strong> 6,800+ lines of character-driven narrative. The Phoenix Project meets accounting firms.
        </div>
        <a href="/case-studies/data-detectives" class="case-link">Full Case Study →</a>
      </article>
      
      <!-- Scroll -->
      <article class="work-card featured">
        <div class="work-tenets">
          <span class="tenet">Story</span>
          <span class="tenet">AI</span>
          <span class="tenet">Clarity</span>
          <span class="tenet">Growth</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Scroll</h2>
        <p class="work-subtitle">A bookshelf for your best ideas</p>
        <p class="work-description">
          A social network for sharing quotes and lessons from books and longform journalism. 
          AI identifies sources, generates "excellent bits" summaries, and builds communities around ideas.
        </p>
        <div class="work-outcome">
          <strong>Outcome:</strong> Complete 2000+ line PRD with 50+ user stories. Ready to build.
        </div>
        <a href="/case-studies/scroll" class="case-link">Full Case Study →</a>
      </article>
      
      <!-- Slice OS -->
      <article class="work-card">
        <div class="work-tenets">
          <span class="tenet">AI</span>
          <span class="tenet">Growth</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Slice OS</h2>
        <p class="work-subtitle">Pizza truck operations, simplified</p>
        <p class="work-description">
          A mobile pizza business was drowning in spreadsheets and WhatsApp chaos.
          I built an operational OS that handles orders, inventory, shift scheduling, and customer comms.
        </p>
        <div class="work-outcome">
          <strong>Outcome:</strong> Real business using it daily. From chaos to clarity in 3 weeks.
        </div>
        <a href="/case-studies/slice-os" class="case-link">Full Case Study →</a>
      </article>
      
      <!-- Zeitgeist -->
      <article class="work-card">
        <div class="work-tenets">
          <span class="tenet">Insight</span>
          <span class="tenet">AI</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Zeitgeist</h2>
        <p class="work-subtitle">Real-time cultural intelligence from 10 sources</p>
        <p class="work-description">
          What's actually happening right now? I built a system that synthesises 
          podcasts, news, research papers, and social signals into one actionable view.
        </p>
        <div class="work-outcome">
          <strong>Outcome:</strong> Pattern detection that surfaces emerging trends before they hit mainstream.
        </div>
      </article>
      
      <!-- Freed Reads -->
      <article class="work-card">
        <div class="work-tenets">
          <span class="tenet">Clarity</span>
          <span class="tenet">Growth</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Freed Reads</h2>
        <p class="work-subtitle">Public domain books, made accessible</p>
        <p class="work-description">
          Thousands of free books exist. Nobody reads them because the experience is terrible.
          I built a daily curation system that surfaces hidden gems with modern presentation.
        </p>
        <div class="work-outcome">
          <strong>Outcome:</strong> Automated pipeline from Gutenberg to beautiful, shareable daily recommendations.
        </div>
        <div class="work-links">
          <a href="/rabbit-holes/signal-from-noise/" class="case-link">Explore the Methodology →</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      
      <!-- Investing Dojo -->
      <article class="work-card">
        <div class="work-tenets">
          <span class="tenet">AI</span>
          <span class="tenet">Clarity</span>
          <span class="tenet">Growth</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Investing Dojo</h2>
        <p class="work-subtitle">Master the markets — White Belt to Black Belt</p>
        <p class="work-description">
          Financial podcasts transcribed, summarised, and transformed into a belt-graded 
          investment curriculum. From beginner basics to advanced mastery.
        </p>
        <div class="work-outcome">
          <strong>Outcome:</strong> 401 articles. 8 belt levels. Live in production.
        </div>
        <div class="work-links">
          <a href="/case-studies/investing-dojo" class="case-link">Full Case Study →</a>
          <a href="https://investingdojo.co/" target="_blank" class="demo-link">Visit Site ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      
      <!-- Club Dadvice -->
      <article class="work-card">
        <div class="work-tenets">
          <span class="tenet">Clarity</span>
          <span class="tenet">AI</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Club Dadvice</h2>
        <p class="work-subtitle">Where dads level up to raise world-class kids</p>
        <p class="work-description">
          Parenting content is everywhere — but mostly for mums. AI-curated wisdom from 
          the best parenting podcasts, framed for fathers.
        </p>
        <div class="work-outcome">
          <strong>Outcome:</strong> 100+ articles. Searchable by challenge. Mobile-first.
        </div>
        <div class="work-links">
          <a href="/case-studies/club-dadvice" class="case-link">Full Case Study →</a>
          <a href="https://dadvice.club/" target="_blank" class="demo-link">Visit Site ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      
      <!-- Staying in Europe -->
      <article class="work-card">
        <div class="work-tenets">
          <span class="tenet">Clarity</span>
          <span class="tenet">AI</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Staying in Europe</h2>
        <p class="work-subtitle">The simplest Schengen calculator for Brits</p>
        <p class="work-description">
          Post-Brexit, British citizens get 90 days in 180. Calculating the rolling window 
          is confusing. This tool does one job perfectly.
        </p>
        <div class="work-outcome">
          <strong>Outcome:</strong> Live utility. Zero friction. Just works.
        </div>
        <div class="work-links">
          <a href="/case-studies/staying-in-europe" class="case-link">Full Case Study →</a>
          <a href="https://www.stayingineurope.com/" target="_blank" class="demo-link">Visit Site ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section cta-section">
    <h2>Got a problem that needs solving?</h2>
    <p>I take on 2 new projects per quarter. Let's see if yours is next.</p>
    <a href="mailto:dave@wordandmouth.com" class="cta-button">Start a Conversation</a>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero-small {
    padding: 10rem 2rem 4rem;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  
  .hero-small h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .hero-small p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  
  .work-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  
  .work-card {
    background: #111;
    padding: 2.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }
  
  .work-tenets {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .tenet {
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.15);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  
  .work-card h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  
  .work-subtitle {
    color: #ccc;
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .work-description {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  
  .work-outcome {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  
  .work-outcome strong {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  
  .demo-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    transition: transform 0.2s;
  }
  
  .demo-link:hover {
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }
  
  .work-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  
  .case-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }
  
  .case-link:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  
  .cta-section {
    text-align: center;
  }
  
  .cta-section h2 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .cta-section p {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
</style>
